<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#lachit-divas">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lachit Divas</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lachit Diwas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lachit Divas is an annual day of commemoration held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on 24 November, the birthday of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lachit-borphukan">Lachit Borphukan</a>, the Ahom general who defeated the Mughal army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-saraighat">Battle of Saraighat</a> in 1671. It is marked by state ceremonies, schools and civic bodies as a celebration of Assamese resistance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, and the best passing-out cadet of India's National Defence Academy receives the Lachit Borphukan gold medal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lachit-divas.jpg" alt="Lachit Divas" width="268" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: বিকাশ দিহিঙ্গীয়া · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Status_of_lachit_borphhukon_and_ahom_sibsagar_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
